        <body>
            <div xml:id="d638">

                <pb facs="0730" n="416" xml:id="pg416"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 165.102/167</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-10-14T13:00:00+01:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">October 14, 1914, 1 p.m.</hi></date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received October 15, 3 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>505. The German Government and exporters must have guarantee our Government that
                    goods shipped on the <hi rendition="#italic">Matanzas</hi> shall not be
                    reexported. I have already suggested in cable of September 26 that Department of
                    Commerce and Labor be charged with duty of seeing that none of goods are used
                    except in the United States and Mexico. Guarantee of individuals and companies
                    not sufficient.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
